168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (With this technique the artist is able to create big amounts of these photographs. Taking the initial material out of the context and adding layers and effects, creating a lot of variations in order to make a new collection that is commenting on the always advancing technology, and mock the absurdity that comes with it. The work itself is now becoming an archive which is always growing. The content of which is the image of a mountain, being a symbol of stability and site of orientation, which is the parallel of the shifting photography medium during the digital age. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (This work is an archive created by an individual, who is using mass produced and publicly available images. Through recontextualising the material and transformation with the use of digital apps, she created an archive which is presented in different formats such as a book, an installation and online publication. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
