175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 113 0 R
/T (The museum having a digital form allowed the creators to experiment in the way they present the objects. Some items appear in a photo format, where it depicts Ukrainian culture, traditions and people, while others take a form of 3D scans. For example, a scanned memorial sign, where the text, despite the low quality of the textures, can be still read. Some elements are almost completely remodeled to match the original appearance. In some cases, artefacts are converted into abstract digital forms, like the mosaics that are turned into VFX particles that are moving. A stained-glass window is digitally translated into a low-poly architectural environment. The material and geometry recreate its real life glass qualities. The museum has a lot of interactive features, where the player can turn on an audio guide, click to read about an item, collect coins as they are exploring the location, creating active engagement with the archival records. )
/E (The museum having a digital form allowed the creators to experiment in the way they present the objects. Some items appear in a photo format, where it depicts Ukrainian culture, traditions and people, while others take a form of 3D scans. For example, a scanned memorial sign, where the text, despite the low quality of the textures, can be still read. Some elements are almost completely remodeled to match the original appearance. In some cases, artefacts are converted into abstract digital forms, like the mosaics that are turned into VFX particles that are moving. A stained-glass window is digitally translated into a low-poly architectural environment. The material and geometry recreate its real life glass qualities. The museum has a lot of interactive features, where the player can turn on an audio guide, click to read about an item, collect coins as they are exploring the location, creating active engagement with the archival records. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
