<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (The archive is openly accessible online, removing the institutional and location restrictions of engaging with the material, which often happens with traditional archives. The accessible, educational and entertaining nature of the archive can help to reach the topic of cultural erasure and war crimes to younger audiences and people from outside of Ukraine.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 114 0 R
/E (The authorship and selection also depart from the traditional archival techniques. The archive is not created by an institution but by individuals and collectives responding to cultural erasure. The content is determined by acts of destruction and theft, instead of traditional archival selection. The archive shifts from imposing an institutional narrative to documenting cultural loss, allowing citizens to reclaim authorship and use it as a political and cultural statement against Russian oppression.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
