186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (In traditional archives that document real places, nature, botanic, or landscapes the goal is to classify, educate and preserve the specific locations and plants within a realistic, systematic way. By keeping and emphasising the technological distortions and gaps, Valla highlights the imperfections of the digitalization processes. The content is now framed around the process of digital capture, instead of fully focusing on natural environments. The archive becomes an artwork that views nature through a subjective contemporary technological view. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 115 0 R
/E (The archive focuses on viewers' aesthetic experience, instead of being informative. The technological art approach changes the way the viewer perceives regular subjects such as nature collection. In this case the work explores a juxtaposition between nature and technology. The process of digitalization becomes as significant as the archived content itself. Demonstrating how unconventional archives prioritise experience, process and interpretation over objectivity and scientific accuracy, while the archive is presented as an aesthetic and conceptual work. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
