193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 116 0 R
/T (The scanned toilet spaces are often viewed as private and unpleasant, and are often overlooked. In traditional archival context, such material would rarely be considered a serious material for preservation. Archives usually prioritise culturally, historically or politically significant material. Welch's project challenges this notion by focusing on everyday spaces that are usually left unnoticed. )
/E (The scanned toilet spaces are often viewed as private and unpleasant, and are often overlooked. In traditional archival context, such material would rarely be considered a serious material for preservation. Archives usually prioritise culturally, historically or politically significant material. Welch's project challenges this notion by focusing on everyday spaces that are usually left unnoticed. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 116 0 R
/T (Through 3D scanning and online publishing the restrooms are detached from the original context and function. The user experiences them as abstract digital objects instead of usable spaces. This detachment is similar to the loss of material context discussed earlier, where the digitalization transforms objects into their representations that are accessed through interfaces. )
/E (Through 3D scanning and online publishing the restrooms are detached from the original context and function. The user experiences them as abstract digital objects instead of usable spaces. This detachment is similar to the loss of material context discussed earlier, where the digitalization transforms objects into their representations that are accessed through interfaces. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
