/P 117 0 R
/E (Learning to Love You More \(2009\) is a web-based project created by artists Miranda July and Harrell Fletcher that is an example of an archive built through public participation. The project invited the general public to respond to simple assignments created by the artists, such as recreating a poster from their teenage years, writing a short life story in less than a day or posting their favourite songs from their childhood. Around eight thousand participants were completing the instructions and attaching a video, text, audio, photographs according to the theme \(July, Fletcher, 2009\). Resulting in an archive containing thousands of personal responses of various people. The work was posted online and the content was presented at different places around the USA.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (Unlike traditional archives where the material exists independently and is later collected, this project was encouraging users to produce the content through the archive. This changes the relationship between the archivists and records, where instead of purposely collecting material for a specific purpose, the project allows the material to be produced without much intervention. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
