>>
endobj
206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (This paper explored how the meaning and function of an archive have shifted in the context of the digital age. Once understood as institutionally controlled physical spaces containing reliable information and records, archives have transformed into a publicly accessible system that is created with digital technologies, online platforms and user participation. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 119 0 R
/T (Through analyses of case studies, this research has shown how artists respond to these limitations by developing unconventional archives. Instead of replicating traditional archival practices, the emerging ones rely on subjectivity, recontextualisation of material and technological use. Artists bring additional narratives, redistribute authorship, experiment with viewer experience and purposes of the archives. Using the archives as a creative medium.)
/E (Through analyses of case studies, this research has shown how artists respond to these limitations by developing unconventional archives. Instead of replicating traditional archival practices, the emerging ones rely on subjectivity, recontextualisation of material and technological use. Artists bring additional narratives, redistribute authorship, experiment with viewer experience and purposes of the archives. Using the archives as a creative medium.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 119 0 R
/T (Unconventional archives offer a more accurate reflection of contemporary informational society, in which data is always produced, modified and circulated. By adapting to these conditions, such archives create space for artistic and cultural expression, critical reinterpretation and alternative ways of engaging with memory and history.)
/E (Unconventional archives offer a more accurate reflection of contemporary informational society, in which data is always produced, modified and circulated. By adapting to these conditions, such archives create space for artistic and cultural expression, critical reinterpretation and alternative ways of engaging with memory and history.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
