/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 104 0 R
/E (This paper argues that the growing amount of unconventional archives shifts institutional control over knowledge and provides a more accurate reflection of contemporary society than traditional archival models.)
/Pg 10 0 R
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 105 0 R
/E (Each archive exists for different purposes, focusing on different types of records. They can preserve material belonging to a specific academic, corporate, governmental, museums, religious, historical institution \(Society of American Archivists, 2025\). Personal archives may hold family relics, objects of value, photos, letters, art objects and more.)
/Pg 11 0 R
>>
endobj
